    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d357">

                <pb facs="0365" n="355" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg355"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/4529</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the British Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Campbell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-09-28">September 28,
                        1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Chargé d’affaires</hi>: I have received
                    your letter of September 9, 1943 in regard to the decision of your Government to
                        <pb facs="0366" n="356" xml:id="pg356"/> accept for onward transport to
                    Palestine all Jews who may succeed in escaping to Turkey from enemy-controlled
                    territory.</p>
                <p>I assume that the British Ambassador at Ankara will be informed of this decision
                    and hope that it will be possible for him to communicate it informally to the
                    American Embassy at Ankara. Such action would be of great assistance in
                    connection with our joint efforts to relieve the sufferings of these unfortunate
                    people.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>A. A. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berle, Jr.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
